# KiCad text formats — diffable as text (also what Prism's semantic diffing
# reads). merge=union stops git from refusing to merge two changed
# schematics, but a unioned S-expression file is still nonsense to open in
# KiCad — this exists to make a conflict an obvious mess someone stops and
# asks about, not to make schematic merges actually work. The real
# protection is the one-owner-at-a-time convention in README.md.
*.kicad_sch text merge=union
*.kicad_pcb text
*.kicad_pro text
*.kicad_wks text
*.kicad_dru text

# Treat as generated/vendored: not shown in language stats, collapsed in
# diffs on GitHub's UI.
Logos/* -diff
*.step -diff -text
*.png -diff -text

# Force LF regardless of a Windows checkout's core.autocrlf setting. A CRLF
# shebang line (#!/bin/bash\r) fails to find the interpreter inside a Linux
# Docker container or CI runner — this bit us running kibot_launch.sh locally
# after checking it out on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
